WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.499
It's now my privilege to sign the

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.079
Homeland Security Act.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:04.289
The Department of Homeland Security

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.209
will have nearly 170,000

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.210
employees.

00:00:08.039 --> 00:00:09.659
The threat of mass murder on our own

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.579
soil will be

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.889
met with a unified, effective

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.239
response.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.409
So the Department of Homeland

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.749
Security, DHS, is celebrating

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.399
its 20th birthday, which is a

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.229
perfect opportunity to rethink

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.729
the whole concept of homeland

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.619
security and how to best

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:26.639
provide it.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.859
DHS has grown into a monster

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.989
child that is massively expensive,

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:32.849
incredibly ineffective and

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.219
reliably destructive of basic

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.479
civil liberties.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.309
It's time to abolish it and

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.139
replace it with fewer, smaller and

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.089
more accountable agencies.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.619
In the wake of the 9/11 attacks,

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.699
President George W.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.169
Bush called for the creation of a

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.299
new Cabinet-level department,

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.309
whose primary mission is to protect

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:51.599
the American homeland.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.129
By pulling border security,

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.199
emergency services and immigration

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.639
into a single, streamlined

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.619
bureaucracy, Bush promised

00:00:58.620 --> 00:00:59.999
that the new department would

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.009
improve efficiency without

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.119
growing government.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.679
Instead, we got politically

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.449
manipulated, color-coded terror

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:08.489
alerts that only made it easier

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:10.139
for late night comedians.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.299
The threat level is now

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.300
magenta.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.619
The DHS budget now stands at

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.539
$82 billion, or

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.279
almost double its original cost in

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.289
inflation-adjusted dollars.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.909
Are there really twice as many

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:25.319
threats to the homeland as there

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.149
were when the embers at Ground

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.189
Zero were still smoldering

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:30.779
and the global war on terror was

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.249
just ramping up.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.049
In the early days of the war on

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:36.029
terror, Washington was obsessed

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.979
with the idea that the 9/11 attacks

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.019
happened because different agencies,

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.969
notably the CIA, FBI

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.129
and NSA, didn't communicate

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:45.299
with each other.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.489
Hence the idea of a unified homeland

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:48.809
security structure.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.699
But critics of DHS noted from

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.289
the start that it didn't actually

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.239
reduce bureaucracy or streamline

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.439
much of anything.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.389
It just added a new layer of red

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:59.249
tape on top of existing

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.529
agencies while creating new ones

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.179
such as the Customs and Border

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.429
Patrol and Immigration and Customs

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:06.899
Enforcement, both of which have

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.999
become legendary for callousness

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.589
and root-level failures.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:12.479
Similarly, the Federal Emergency

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.369
Management Agency, FEMA,

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.019
has gone from catastrophic failure

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.579
in New Orleans all the way to

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.889
catastrophic failure in Puerto Rico,

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:22.049
updating its long standing, stumble

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:24.269
bum reputation for the 21st

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.049
century.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:26.489
In a new report, FEMA admits

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.349
failures occurred in its disaster

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.449
response to Hurricane Maria.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.489
A 2019 inspector general

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.349
report called out DHS

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:36.959
for failing to rein in bad behavior,

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.519
ranging from padding expense

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.379
accounts to drinking on the job

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.329
to illegal reprisals against

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.579
sexual harassment whistleblowers.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.259
The report concluded no one was

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.939
really in charge of organizing and

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:49.679
inspecting reports of employee

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:50.549
misbehavior.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.799
President Biden has boasted that DHS

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.779
has almost 260,000

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.639
employees, yet its H.R.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.289
department told the inspector

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.209
general it had limited staffing

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:02.069
to perform these functions, and

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:03.479
staff do not believe they are

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.919
responsible for managing the

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.269
allegation process.

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:08.699
Perhaps worst of all, DHS

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.769
is a determined foe of civil

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:11.609
liberties.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.439
As the ACLU documents in a

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:14.524
new study of the department, DHS

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.969
routinely undermines our ability

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:19.859
to speak and move freely about the

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.869
very country it's supposed

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:22.799
to be protecting.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.299
For instance, since immigration

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.589
enforcement became part of a

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:27.629
national security agenda,

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.149
ICE agents encourage local police

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.189
to stop, arrest and bring low-level

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:34.199
charges against people who look like

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.149
immigrants, with the actual aim

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.949
of helping ICE deport them.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.659
Looking like an immigrant isn't

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.579
against the law, and it shouldn't be

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.199
a pretext for a police stop.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.149
And when we talk about DHS, of

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.769
course we have to talk about the

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:48.599
Transportation Security

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.600
Administration, TSA.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.649
Oh, curse the brilliant

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:53.759
TSA!

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.199
Which you might refer to as

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.639
"Thousands Standing Around," the

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.469
"Testicle Squeezing Agency"

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.089
or any number of different

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:00.899
euphemisms.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.939
Despite very occasional positive

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:04.919
headlines, the TSA rightly

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.239
looms large in the public

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.219
imagination as a make-work

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.409
program gone horribly wrong.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.209
Famous for forcing mothers to drink

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.859
their own breast milk, scaring

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.049
children and panting the elderly,

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:17.999
the TSA reportedly spends as

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.419
much as $667 billion

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:22.949
per life saved.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.989
On its 10th anniversary, two

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:26.639
conservative Republican members of

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:29.309
Congress even denounced the TSA,

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.139
saying the degraded security

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:33.329
theater it imposed on travelers

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.459
did not improve on the safety

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.289
protocols that were in place before

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.189
9/11.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:40.319
DHS's mission is simply

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:42.029
too vast to accomplish.

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:43.829
Having been tasked to do so many

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:45.779
different things, from processing

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:47.489
immigration checks, to responding to

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.349
natural disasters, to checking

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:50.759
passengers on every flight in

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.699
America, to stopping terrorism,

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:55.559
it ends up doing all of them

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.489
poorly.

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:57.899
It would be better to break those

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.109
functions up into smaller agencies

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.699
that are directly accountable to

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.409
departments that existed prior to

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.549
9/11.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:05.598
As Richard A.

00:05:05.599 --> 00:05:07.129
Clarke, a 30 year veteran of

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.899
security positions in the Defense

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:10.219
Department, State Department and

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.139
White House, has suggested

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:13.819
it makes sense to create a smaller

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:15.499
group, tightly focused on

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.359
terroristic threats that would

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.279
work directly with the FBI and the

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:21.259
Office of National Intelligence.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:22.759
"Preserving the status quo," he

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.739
writes, "will only perpetuate

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:26.179
the mistakes made in the panic

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:28.009
trauma that followed 911

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:30.139
and doom these important missions

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.969
to continued mishandling and

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:34.249
lack of success." As it celebrates

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:36.229
its 20th birthday, its

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.750
time to blow out the candles on DHS.

